EXT. ROOFTOP WATER TANK - SUNSET

A battered rooftop, tar-papered and patched. A wooden water tank on stilts casts a long shadow. Pigeons coo. Beyond the parapet, the city glows orange.

Three teenagers sit with their legs hanging over the edge: MALIK "MO" JOHNSON (17, backwards cap), GABRIELA "GABBY" ORTEGA-NG (16, cut-off jean jacket), and SIMON "SI" DELACROIX-ODUYA (17, oversized glasses, a handheld camera).

MO
So that's it. Last summer.

GABBY
It's not the last summer.

MO
It's the last summer we're all in the same city.

SI
You don't know that.

MO
Gabby's going to Toronto.

GABBY
Maybe.

MO
You got the letter.

GABBY
I got a letter.

SI
What did it say?

GABBY
It said yes.

MO
Then it's Toronto.

GABBY
It's a maybe, Mo.

SI
(filming)
Say it again for the camera.

GABBY
Si, turn that off.

SI
It's my documentary.

GABBY
It's my life.

SI
(lowering the camera)
Sorry.

MO
You could stay.

GABBY
And do what?

MO
Same as always.

GABBY
That's the problem.

A long beat. A pigeon lands on the tank, bobs its head, flies away.

SI
I got into film school.

MO
You what?

SI
In L.A. I haven't told my parents.

MO
Si! That's huge!

SI
It's a thousand miles away.

GABBY
So is Toronto.

MO
So you're both leaving.

SI
I didn't say that.

GABBY
You did.

SI
I said I got in.

MO
What about me?

GABBY
What about you?

MO
I'm not going anywhere.

SI
You could.

MO
To where?

GABBY
Anywhere.

MO
I don't want anywhere. I want here.

SI
Here is changing, Mo.

MO
Here is fine.

GABBY
Here is a rooftop.

MO
It's a good rooftop.

They laugh, thin and tired. The sun slides lower. Their shadows stretch across the tar.

SI
Let's film the sunset.

GABBY
Then it's real.

SI
It's already real.

MO
Do it.

Si lifts the camera. Pans across the skyline. Settles on the two of them.

SI
Say something. For the archive.

GABBY
Hi. We were here.

MO
(softly)
We were here.

The sun touches the horizon. The camera keeps rolling.
